     * For each lead, returns the Id of the first contact (in contacts order)
     * whose email matches the lead's email (ignoring case and surrounding
     * whitespace), or null. A blank/null email never matches.
     *
     * Uses a normalised-email to Id map so the method is O(leads + contacts)
     * rather than O(leads x contacts). At the stated maxima (3k x 3k) this
     * keeps CPU usage negligible inside the import transaction.
     *
     * This method performs no DML or SOQL.
