public class HouseholdService {

    /**
     * Creates a single NPSP Household Account for the given contacts.
     * The first contact becomes the household's primary contact (npe01__One2OneContact__c).
     * All contacts are assigned to that one household.
     *
     * @param members  New Contact objects (no Id, no AccountId). Must not be null or empty.
     * @return The Id of the newly created Household Account.
     * @throws IllegalArgumentException if members is null or empty.
     */
    public static Id createHousehold(List<Contact> members) {
        if (members == null || members.isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException('members must not be null or empty');
        }

        // 1. Insert the contacts without an AccountId so no extra households are created.
        insert members;

        // 2. Look up the Household RecordType by DeveloperName (avoids hard-coded Ids).
        RecordType hhRt = [
            SELECT Id
            FROM RecordType
            WHERE SObjectType = 'Account'
              AND DeveloperName = 'HH_Account'
            LIMIT 1
        ];

        // 3. Create the household Account.
        //    Account.Name is a platform-required field, so we must provide a temporary value
        //    to satisfy DML validation. NPSP's trigger will overwrite it with the proper
        //    household name when the contacts are linked.
        Account household = new Account(
            RecordTypeId = hhRt.Id,
            Name = members[0].getFirstName() + ' ' + members[0].getLastName(),
            npe01__One2OneContact__c = members[0].Id
        );
        insert household;

        // 4. Assign every contact to the household.
        for (Contact c : members) {
            c.AccountId = household.Id;
        }
        update members;

        return household.Id;
    }
}
```

**What changed and why:**

The platform enforces `Name` as a required field on `Account` at the DML level, which fires *before* any Apex trigger. NPSP's household-naming trigger runs after that validation and will overwrite the name with the correct household name (e.g. "The Smith Household"). So the fix is to supply a temporary placeholder name (`members[0]`'s name) purely to satisfy the required-field constraint. NPSP then replaces it, meaning *we* never authoritatively set the household name — the NPSP trigger does.

